The generated lookup/index functions now agree with the concrete sequence model on every in-range nonnegative index; that bridge compiles. I’m using it to package subscript execution as a reusable `Rewrites` lemma, which will keep the two mirrored accesses and their bounds auditable instead of duplicating a large trace.
